      "description": "Original MIT synthetic images and projects, generated by build_example.py. No customer or third-party images. Three white circles have known centers and a fixed radius. APNG and lossless WebP must return exact visible samples in order at 80/120/200 ms. GIF reduces color and uses 10-ms timing: 83/129/208 explicitly quantizes to 80/120/200. The exact GIF timing example intentionally rejects those durations and emits nothing. The inspection project unbatches all three frames into ordinary image tools; the last visible result is frame 2 at x=116. One file acquisition ticket owns the group, with frame indices/timing on each image. Writer output never replaces an existing file. These are bounded offline data transformations; display playback pacing is not added.",
